HOW TO READ THIS:
  * 'outer used' > 1 means the solver had to RE-ASSEMBLE to satisfy its own boundary
    condition -- i.e. one assembly was not self-consistent. That is the lag.
  * 'BC residual' is the boundary condition's own definition evaluated on the field
    actually returned. It is 0 by construction for FixedGradient whenever the face
    value is reconstructed FROM the owner, so it measures self-consistency of the
    returned field, NOT whether the assembled flux used a stale value.
  * the discriminating number is therefore 'outer used' at maxOuter=2000, compared
    between species and thermal on the identical problem shape.
